summary:
  The title reader takes a certificate whose subject's CN names the host and
  which has no subjectAltName.

history:
  The context the dates are let go in is Python's default, which still lets
  the CN stand in for a missing subjectAltName; requests' own context does
  not. Without the line the reader accepted more than a lapsed date.

target:
  package/contents/ui/reader.py

find:
      ctx.hostname_checks_common_name = False

replace:
      ctx.hostname_checks_common_name = True

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_reader_tls.py::test_a_host_named_only_in_the_common_name_is_still_refused.
  Line-neutral.
